An application stores an RSA key named app-signing-key in an Azure key vault. Contoso's cryptographic standard requires that the key be rotated automatically every 12 months without any administrator action, and that the platform team receive a notification 30 days before the key's expiry date so they can validate that consuming applications pick up the new version.

What should you configure on the key vault?

回答は正解です
A key rotation policy on app-signing-key that rotates the key every 12 months, together with a near-expiry event notification delivered through Azure Event Grid.
説明
This answer is correct. A key rotation policy is defined per key and instructs Key Vault to generate a new key version automatically on the schedule you specify. Key Vault also publishes near-expiry events to Azure Event Grid, so a subscription on that event can notify the platform team ahead of the expiry date.
An Azure Policy assignment that audits keys older than 12 months.
説明
This answer is incorrect. An audit policy reports on keys that have exceeded the age threshold after the fact. It neither rotates the key nor warns the team in advance of expiry.
Purge protection with a 90-day soft-delete retention period.
説明
This answer is incorrect. Purge protection prevents permanent deletion of vault objects during the retention window. It plays no part in generating new key versions or in producing expiry notifications.
An Azure Automation runbook scheduled annually that creates a new key version.
説明
This answer is incorrect. A runbook can technically create key versions, but it duplicates a native Key Vault feature and adds credentials, code, and failure modes to maintain. It also provides no near-expiry notification without further custom development.
全体的な説明
Azure Key Vault supports rotation policies at the level of an individual key, which define both the rotation interval and the expiry time for each generated version. When the policy fires, Key Vault creates a new version of the key while retaining previous versions, so applications referencing the versionless key identifier pick up the new material automatically. Key Vault also emits lifecycle events to Azure Event Grid, including a near-expiry event that can be configured to fire a set number of days before expiry and routed to email, Logic Apps, or a webhook. Together these two features satisfy the standard without any scheduled scripts or manual intervention. Purge protection and audit policies address deletion resilience and reporting respectively, neither of which performs rotation.
